## AI Agents

| Agent | What It Analyzes |
|-------|-----------------|
| Software Tester | Tool errors, usage patterns, broken tools |
| UI/UX Researcher | User flows, feature discovery, UX friction |
| Customer Support | FAQ generation, response templates |
| Site Reliability Engineer | Error rates, capacity, system health |
| Data Analyst | Usage trends, revenue insights, anomalies |
| Growth Analyst | Acquisition, conversion, growth trajectory |
| Student ID Verifier | Student plan verification, fraud patterns |
| Security Auditor | Suspicious activity, access pattern analysis |

## Dashboards

| Dashboard | Key Metrics |
|-----------|------------|
| Overview | Total users, premium, revenue, tool usage, system status |
| Growth | DAU, MAU, daily signups, new vs recurring, top tools |
| Revenue | MRR, ARR, conversion, churn, LTV, CAC, plan distribution |
| Retention | D1/3/7/14/30 cohort curve, DAU trend |
| Funnel | Visitor → Signup → Tool Use → Premium conversion |
| Infra | Hourly requests, error rate, endpoint health, latency |
| Cost | Cloud spend, cost/user, LTV:CAC, compute utilization |
| Frontend | Core Web Vitals (LCP/FID/CLS), page load times |
| Users | Premium vs free breakdown, tool usage comparison |

---

## Verification Results

- ✅ **Build**: `npm run build` — exit code 0, all 15 routes compiled
- ✅ **Auth Gate**: Wrong key → error, correct key → redirect to dashboard
- ✅ **All 10 dashboards** load with real Supabase data
- ✅ **Agent Control**: 8 agents with toggles and Run buttons

---

## Deploy to Vercel

```bash
cd admin-dashboard
npx vercel --prod
```

**Environment variables to set in Vercel:**

| Variable | Value |
|----------|-------|
| `ADMIN_SECRET_KEY` | `HarshNishaAnayaVivek` |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` | Your Supabase URL |
| `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` | Your Supabase service key |
| `GROQ_API_KEY` | Your Groq API key |

## Database Setup

Run [admin-schema.sql](file:///c:/Users/admin/Desktop/Duxport-new/duxport/admin-dashboard/admin-schema.sql) in Supabase SQL Editor to create the agent tracking tables.
